Guidelines for Jetpack Compose Testing in Android
Use JUnit for unit tests and Espresso for UI tests to ensure structured and reliable testing.
Add Compose testing dependencies in build.gradle for proper test execution.
Use createComposeRule() in test classes to manage Compose UI tests efficiently.
Leverage Semantics (onNodeWithText(), onNodeWithTag()) instead of findViewById().
Assign Modifier.testTag() to non-text elements for easy identification in tests.
Use awaitIdle() and waitForIdle() to ensure UI updates are complete before assertions.
Use runTest for coroutine-based ViewModel tests to handle asynchronous operations correctly.
Simulate gestures (performClick(), performScrollTo(), performTextInput()) for UI interactions.
